sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Staff as IT Support Staff
    participant Client as React Client (TicketDetail)
    participant AuthMw as Auth Middleware
    participant TicketCtrl as Tickets Controller
    participant Rules as Ticket Rules (ticketRules.js)
    participant TicketModel as Ticket Model (MongoDB)
    participant Audit as Audit Service (logAudit)

    Staff->>Client: Selects "RESOLVED", inputs resolution notes, clicks "Update Status"
    Client->>AuthMw: PATCH /api/v1/tickets/:id/status { status: 'RESOLVED', resolutionNote } [Bearer JWT]

    AuthMw->>AuthMw: Authenticate token & authorize IT_SUPPORT role
    AuthMw->>TicketCtrl: updateTicketStatus(req, res, next)

    TicketCtrl->>TicketModel: Ticket.findById(ticketId)
    TicketModel-->>TicketCtrl: Return ticket document (status: 'IN_PROGRESS')

    TicketCtrl->>Rules: canTransition('IN_PROGRESS', 'RESOLVED')
    Rules-->>TicketCtrl: true (valid state progression)

    TicketCtrl->>TicketCtrl: Validate resolutionNote length >= 5 characters

    TicketCtrl->>TicketModel: findByIdAndUpdate(ticketId, { status: 'RESOLVED', resolutionNote, resolvedAt: now }, { new: true })
    TicketModel-->>TicketCtrl: Return updated ticket

    TicketCtrl->>Audit: logAudit(TICKET_STATUS, 'from IN_PROGRESS to RESOLVED', ticketId)
    Audit-->>TicketCtrl: Audit persisted

    TicketCtrl-->>Client: 200 OK { success: true, data: updatedTicket }
    Client->>Client: showToast('Ticket status updated to RESOLVED', 'success')
    Client-->>Staff: Render green RESOLVED badge and resolution notes card
